        "line": 3,
        "text": "**Date:** 2026-10-17. **Status:** proposed extensions; none of the new exports claimed shipped. **Branch:** main. **Canonical program:** [Adaptive Computation and Control](https://github.com/jehalladay/FiberOpticsResearch/tree/main/docs/research/foa/programs/adaptive-computation-and-control-2026-10-17). **Work packages:** AC-01, AC-04, AC-10, AC-15.",
        "sha256": "ec7457829e2137aefb8e88f4451d1155db1d93bf002cd58d6de8b2c1cefef58b"
      },
      {
        "line": 66,
        "text": "ActivityBoundary ACTIVE/WARM/DORMANT/EVICTED remains separate from QueryView identity and speculative execution ownership. A warm context may precompute only explicitly eligible read-only resources under existing SpeculationBoundary, not call inference/effects. Add tests TSX-RQ1 five-stage TestHealth, TSX-RQ2 ready UNKNOWN vs pending, TSX-RQ3 aborted attempt no registration, TSX-RQ4 query spec scope changes stable hook order, TSX-RQ5 two consumers share one host query view without premature unsubscribe, TSX-RQ6 TS/Python golden, TSX-RQ7 existing ADR-0032 no premature optimizer or component skipping. DevTools only consumes emitted host events.",
        "sha256": "844542075747acc40157ebf5078077036f308a65c3726caa11d455de66ed00f6"
      }
    ],
